# Frontend And API Routes

- Follow `AGENTS.md` and keep server-only logic out of client components.
- Client components must not import service-role Supabase, credential services, encryption modules, Node-only SDKs, or secret-bearing env vars.
- Contractor-facing API routes should authenticate with `lib/auth/session.js` and scope by `company_id`.
- Admin-only routes must call `requireSuperAdmin()` or an equivalent verified check before service-role reads/writes.
- Do not trust client-supplied `company_id`, job IDs, run IDs, or storage paths without server-side ownership checks.
- The contractor chat widget is not working unless server-side `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is configured. Never expose that key or any AI/provider secret to browser code.
- Do not reintroduce the removed contractor materials tab/system.
- Validate UI/API changes with relevant `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, and safe route/module tests. Do not call live webhooks or external portals for validation.
